From 702d44289fbb8628661cb76b5ba96191a1afd820 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 361/488] soh: name the 21 address-named symbols defined in
 z_bg_spot16_bombstone.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 21 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Bg_Spot16_Bombstone/z_bg_spot16_bombstone.c.

  * func_808B4C30 -> BgSpot16Bombstone_SplitParams
    deduced, confidence HIGH: pulls the switch flag out of the high byte of
    params and leaves the type in the low byte

  * func_808B4C4C -> BgSpot16Bombstone_InitJntSphCollider
    deduced, confidence HIGH: builds the 120-unit jntsph centred 50 units
    above the boulder

  * func_808B4D04 -> BgSpot16Bombstone_InitCylinderCollider
    deduced, confidence HIGH: builds the cylinder collider and offsets it to
    world position

  * func_808B4D9C -> BgSpot16Bombstone_InitBoulder
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the params 0 branch of Init: returns false
    when the switch flag is already set, otherwise sets up the boulder's
    scale, colliders and idle action

  * func_808B4E58 -> BgSpot16Bombstone_InitDebris
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the debris branch of Init: reads this piece's
    row out of sDebrisInits and waits on the bombiwa object

  * func_808B5240 -> BgSpot16Bombstone_SpawnTimedDust
    deduced, confidence HIGH: walks sExplosionDustScript, spawning each
    row's dust puff once the timer reaches its frame

  * func_808B561C -> BgSpot16Bombstone_SpawnDebris
    deduced, confidence HIGH: spawns one child bombstone per entry of
    sDebrisParams

  * func_808B56BC -> BgSpot16Bombstone_PushPlayerAway
    deduced, confidence HIGH: shoves the player back out along the boulder's
    facing when they stand inside it

  * func_808B57E0 -> BgSpot16Bombstone_WatchPlayerBomb
    deduced, confidence HIGH: tracks the bomb flower the player carries and
    opens the one-point cutscene when it is about to go off near the cavern
    entrance

  * func_808B5934 -> BgSpot16Bombstone_SetupIdle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: restores the draw function and installs the
    idle action

  * func_808B5950 -> BgSpot16Bombstone_Idle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: pushes the player out, watches their bomb, and
    on AC_HIT spawns the debris, sets the switch and event flags and blows
    up

  * func_808B5A78 -> BgSpot16Bombstone_SetupExplode
    deduced, confidence HIGH: clears the timers, drops the draw function and
    installs the explosion action

  * func_808B5A94 -> BgSpot16Bombstone_Explode
    deduced, confidence HIGH: runs the dust script, chimes at frame 56 and
    kills the actor after 60

  * func_808B5AF0 -> BgSpot16Bombstone_SetupWaitForObject
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs the wait action and hides the piece
    until the bombiwa object arrives

  * func_808B5B04 -> BgSpot16Bombstone_WaitForObject
    deduced, confidence HIGH: holds until the bombiwa object is loaded, then
    starts the debris flight

  * func_808B5B58 -> BgSpot16Bombstone_SetupFly
    deduced, confidence HIGH: zeroes the flight timer and installs the
    debris flight action

  * func_808B5B6C -> BgSpot16Bombstone_Fly
    deduced, confidence HIGH: arcs the debris under gravity, tumbling it,
    and shatters it into kakera and dust on landing

  * D_808B5DD8 -> sDebrisInits
    deduced, confidence HIGH: one ten-value row per debris params: speed, y
    velocity, scale, the two tumble rates, yaw, height and the three shape
    rotations

  * D_808B5EB0 -> sExplosionDustScript
    deduced, confidence HIGH: rows of frame, x, y, z, scale, scale step and
    life driving BgSpot16Bombstone_SpawnTimedDust

  * D_808B6074 -> sFragmentScales
    deduced, confidence HIGH: per-fragment scale factors for the
    EffectSsKakera shards

  * D_808B6088 -> sDebrisParams
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the params values
    BgSpot16Bombstone_SpawnDebris passes to each spawned piece

